{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/803663-problem-with-religion-based-covenants-lancea-and-circle","id":803663,"title":"Problem with religion based covenants (Lancea and Circle).","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-08T04:59:37-08:00","id":803663,"title":"Problem with religion based covenants (Lancea and Circle).","content":"In the last 18 months I have organized a long term Requiem campaign and 3 other introductory 2-3 sessions mini chronicles for different groups. All games took place in a big city with about 60-70 kindred. Combining all players, and considering their chosen covenant I had this character distribution:<br /> <br /> Ordo: 7 (1 defected to the Invictus)<br /> Invictus: 2 (plus 2 deserters from other covenants)<br /> Carthians: 2<br /> Lancea: 1<br /> Circle: 1 (defected to the Invictus after selling the cult to the Lancea)<br /> <br /> Well, as we can see the Ordo is pretty popular among players, perhaps too much for a lesser young covenant. But that\u2019s ok, no problem. My problem is with the 2 religious Covenants. I literally had to sell them to the players because they were discarded in the first round, not even considered. After some marketing I got a lone Lancea player and a Crone one.<br /> <br /> The Lancea player at least was happy with his character and the covenant. He understood what they were doing, liked Theban sorcery and were in good standing with other Lancea NPCs.<br /> <br /> <br /> But the Crone player... never liked the cult (and she played the long chronicle). I tried to sell the Circle as better as I could, I made the witches able to work spells and summonings much more powerful than the ones you can find in the book. And also after a few moths made the covenant much more politically aggressive. Nothing worked, the player never felt involved, in fact I wasn\u00b4t able to convince her to spend a single experience in cruac. They were \u201ca bunch of crazy ladies in the forest\u201d, my attempts to make the five witches appealing were all in vain.<br /> A lot of wasted work.<br /> <br /> Right now, I\u00b4m developing another city, a much smaller one, about 15 kindred. And I\u00b4m thinking in completely ignoring the Circle and reducing the Lancea to a small cult of one priest and a few Invictus and Carthian sympathizers. I don\u00b4t know if the problem is the non religious times we live, if religion and vampires don\u00b4t mix well or if the problem is mine, because in my deep soul, I don\u00b4t like those covenants and I\u00b4m unable to make them alluring to the players.<br /> <br /> I feel the Ordo got all the appealing \u201csupernatural secret lore\u201d thing the Tremere had in Masquerade, leaving the circle with the bloody hippies concept. And the savage predators stuff, well, all covenants are composed by vampires and all of them are true badasses. And If a vampire don\u00b4t want any rules, he doesn\u00b4t need to follow a forgotten summerian god to be free.<br /> <br /> I can discard the Lancea, but I really like the \u201cblood magic\u201d concept, even if the rituals in the basic rulebook fail to attract players. So I have this options:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Give the sorcery to the Ordo. But would be a bad idea because it already have the coils and has enough sexappeal.</li> <li>\u201cTremerize\u201d the circle. Remove the cult roots and change them a for groups of kindred using the power of the blood and the beast to practice secret sorcery. Change the ritual names to make then more arcane and bookish. Change the bloody forest bacchanals for bloody rituals in a runic magic circle. They wouldn\u2019t pray for magic, they would steal, study and corrupt it. The leaders wouldn\u00b4t be priestess and hierophants, but master sorcerers.</li> <li>Ask for help in the forum. Anybody has found the same problem?, do you have some more modern looking cults? (all this greek, celtic and voodoo stuff hasn\u2019t worked for me). Perhaps more \u201cGod machinish\u201d.</li> </ol><br /> I wouldn\u2019t like to reduce the game to 3 covenants, but I also don\u2019t like to work in vain designing characters and plots that will be ignored by the players. All comments and insight will be wellcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3008-masa","name":"Masa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3008_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T05:16:54-08:00","id":803673,"title":"","content":"Players don't need to be covenants. And you can have the covenants acting in the setting without the players being members of them.<br /> <br /> I'm usually of the mind that if you have to try and convince a player to do something, it's because it's something they don't want to do. In that case, spicing it up isn't going to really change their mind.<br /> <br /> If you haven't started, why not just let the players be the covenants they wanted to in the first place?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T05:36:10-08:00","id":803680,"title":"","content":"I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> on this one.<br /> The Circle and Lancea covenants appeal to a set of players, if none of your players liked then, there's no need to try change the covenant for the players.<br /> As an example, \u200bI find the Circle particularly interesting. \u200bBecause of Cru\u00e1c.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T05:37:29-08:00","id":803681,"title":"","content":"Why not just focus on the Ordo? I mean, 15 is a small place, maybe it's just dominated by one covenant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don\u00b4t know if the problem is the non religious times we live, if religion and vampires don\u00b4t mix well </div> </div> </div>The thing I keep in mind is that kindred existence is really tough. You were human but now you're a cannibalistic corpse who lives off other humans. That's not something you easily ajust to. The two religious covenants are at their base about giving meaning to that existence. I'd compare it to the religiosity you see among prisoners or the homeless (or if you want to go back a bit slaves). If you're at the very bottom of society, it's very appealing to believe there's some divine order or purpose to what's happening to you.<br /> <br /> Personally, I kinda find the magic stuff a bit distracting from that core element.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T06:09:13-08:00","id":803688,"title":"","content":"There's a simple way to run the Circle to be more player-friendly, especially in a tiny location.<br /> <br /> Let the players decide on the cult structure. The amazing thing, to me, about the Circle is the variety of it. At it's core, it's a religious group that exalts the Beast and uses blood sorcery. You can frame it as witches, animists and pagans, you can even frame it in terms of existing religions. Haitian Vodou has a lot of Catholicism in there, for one thing. They could take a more philosophical 'way of living' approach rather than an explicitly religious one. Cruac rites will always involve blood, but they can be ecstatic or somber. As long as they still with the absolute core principles of the Circle and Cruac, let them make whatever crazy cult they want.<br /> <br /> I reckon this approach with really appeal to certain players and is also a way to really integrate the Circle into your city, since the 'default' flavour might not fit..<br /> <br /> You can do something similar with the Lancea, somewhat, but you can't really drop the 'Vampire funhouse mirror reflection of Christianity' thing, which some people flat-out won't be interested in. But there's scope for corrupt, 'God is on my side, so I'm right' zealotry and nastiness, sympathetic (and possibly politically neutral) 'Beasts we are lest beasts we become' guides and gurus, tight-lipped and insular Christian-magicians who appear more like a Masonic Lodge. Again, if you want to use them look at your city and what role you think they'd fit best.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":452,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","user":"Eremite","date":". 01-08-2016, 09:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T06:19:33-08:00","id":803692,"title":"","content":"I'd just let it go. You've got an entire covenant to yourself you can play with. Have the city's Circle be doing some crazy apocalyptic ritual behind closed doors or something. You want your players to like the Crones? Show them what they can do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T07:19:23-08:00","id":803726,"title":"","content":"Weird. The Circle is my absolute favorite Covenant. It's the only one that is about accepting your Vampiric state for what it is, rather than pretending to be something you aren't. The Sanctum try to cope by claiming a mission from God. The Ordo try to cope by changing what they are. The Invictus try to cope by clinging to the trappings of civilization, similar to the Carthains. The Crone just seem very self-accepting, which can be attractive.<br /> <br /> That said, the others are right. There's really no reason you need to have players represent all the Covenants if they aren't into it. Gives you more freedom as Storyteller if they don't, in fact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T08:42:04-08:00","id":803767,"title":"","content":"Add me to the people saying to just let it go. However, I will add that this is a great time to portray attractive NPCs from those covenants. Make their philosophies shine and have those NPCs have sensible, compelling arguments or just be cool/decent folk (by vampire standards).<br /> <br /> You might set up the players to create characters of those covenants next time or even or even convert in this game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T09:18:56-08:00","id":803798,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't go out of my way to make any covenant more attractive rules-wise. Either the players can relate to the underlying philosophy or they can't. But I would refrain from any changes just to get a player to play a member of a specific covenant.<br /> <br /> I have similar experiences with the Circle. None of the players really wanted their characters to belong to the &quot;crazy&quot; blood witches. I continued to portray them faithfully to the fiction. They are my covenant after all - and not because of Cruac, but because of the philosophy they espouse. They are the least civilized and rational of all the covenants, prone to decisions guided by faith and believe not political calculation. It's something rather hard to grasp for most players today, I guess. Especially compared to more easily understood covenants like Carthians and Invictus or the Ordo Dracul who offers tangibel mechanical benefits in dealing with the unpleasant side effects of being a vampire.<br /> <br /> My players chose the Ordo Dracul most often, Invictus second, then Carthians and only rarely Lancea Sanctum and never Circle of the Crone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1681-murder-of-crows","name":"Murder-of-Crows","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1681_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T11:04:40-08:00","id":803854,"title":"","content":"I have issues with new sanctified. The 1st edition I understood. <br /> I like the first Edition Crone not sure about the 2nd.<br /> I agree with others let it go and use them as NPC's<br /> <br /> An example, in the National LARP a certain city came under an ST who did not like the OWOD Nos. So when I and another player visited there were no PC nos.<br /> Well we interacted with several ST NOs characters(good ones too), to get clues about something that troubling local kindred. Apparently we impressed a few players up there. The next time we visited some Ventrue &amp; Torrie players had dropped those characters and built a very well done nos brood led by an elder no less.<br /> <br /> Moral: Show them some interest Crone or Sanctfied characters in action","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T12:06:19-08:00","id":803907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/803663-problem-with-religion-based-covenants-lancea-and-circle?p=803692#post803692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd just let it go.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/803663-problem-with-religion-based-covenants-lancea-and-circle?p=803767#post803767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Add me to the people saying to just let it go.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://memecrunch.com/meme/1T411/the-cold-never-bothered-me-anyway/image.png?w=500&amp;c=1\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 01-08-2016, 03:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T12:38:19-08:00","id":803937,"title":"","content":"Why do you guys assume an Acolyte only focus on his religion? or that he cannot become a corrupt, hypocrital politician disguised under the mask of faith, just like any Sanctified?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T13:17:03-08:00","id":803968,"title":"","content":"The problem with religious based covenants is that every covenant is religious in some way, including the Carthians, Ordo, and Invictus!<br /> <br /> More seriously, there's lots of potential reasons why your players aren't interested. The Lance and Circle could very well be unattractive simply because the players don't want ritual magic! The very thing you are interested in seems to be the thign that your players are least interested in.<br /> <br /> So, perhaps you should have this conversation with your group. Find out what themes they're interested in playing, and what they're not. Hells, given the overwhelming support for the Ordo Dracul, perhaps you should just abandon any attempts at a cosmopolitan game, and just run Ordo Dracul focused plots. Use VII and the Brood (dark enlightenment version, not idiot raver version) as foils. Use the strix as demonic temptations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 01-08-2016, 04:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T14:16:30-08:00","id":803993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/803663-problem-with-religion-based-covenants-lancea-and-circle?p=803937#post803937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do you guys assume an Acolyte only focus on his religion? or that he cannot become a corrupt, hypocrital politician disguised under the mask of faith, just like any Sanctified?</div> </div> </div> </div>The number 2 on the Circle as detailed in Chicago had no dots in Cruac, yet she could compel a crowd like only a Daeva elder can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T15:24:17-08:00","id":804055,"title":"","content":"No Covenant is essential to the Requiem: if the Crone doesn't click with you, the players, or anything you plan to do, drop it. You could fold it or Cruac into the Lancea as a pagan or antinomian branch for later use. Take a look at the settings chapter of V2E, as there are plenty of cities where some covenants aren't represented in any recognizable form. Give Cruac to the Brood, or VII. Run the Circle like a Werewolf pack, full of blood and violence and pagan mysticism, and replace every reference to Wolf and Moon to the Crone. Just leave the Crone as is, and let the players investigate it out ignore it as they see fit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T18:16:46-08:00","id":804161,"title":"","content":"I believe it is not intrinsically tied to the Covenant itself, as it was pointed out that it is very much liked by some players (myself included)<br /> My guess'd be that the Cronites weren't all that appealing because you have focused on presenting raw power they can give, without considring that every Covenant has something to offer in its place, often more powerful than blood sorcery costing precious XPs.<br /> <br /> It is very true that the Circle has to overcome its un-cool apeal of savages, diablerists and &quot;old ladies in the forest&quot;. Who in our world has to do just that too?<br /> That's right, modern sects, particularly satanism. These groups don't entice people by saying that they will perform miracles, rather, they offer a sense of belonging, the feeling that someone has truly got your back. Of course, the Sanctified try to do that too, but if you are not particularly into having your undead butt kicked around by pretty much everyone or being constantly told that you are guilty of a mortal sin by the simple fact of your existence, then it is not the wisest choice. And the Ordo? Please, even themseves can barely understand all that mystical mumbo-jumbo and they confuse surpassing one's nature with defying it.<br /> <br /> The Cronites, however, can give you all the answers and learning environment you can take. No slaves or masters or stupid, millenia-old rules no one even cares to explain. And most importantly: you get to accept who you are now and really make sense of the Beast, the thing that bothers every Kindred in existence. And if you learn some cool rituals along the way? Great, tearing your enemies' throats with your teeth is so much fun!<br /> <br /> Moreover, you do not have to spend the rest of your unlife in some cave to get all that. No, you get to frequent the BEST parties, take the BEST drugs and have the BEST sexual experience you can imagine, because the Cronites know that sensuality is one of the most important parts of a sentient being. Forget all those boring Sanctified monks or stuck-up Ordo mentors - they keep you from it because they know that once someone tastes freedom, he will never again take their shit seriously.<br /> <br /> That way, you have the profit AND pleasure. If NPC the players care about are Cronites too, all the better. Believe me, portraying the Circle in my chronicle that way has worked wonders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10396-woland","name":"Woland","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10396_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T03:54:16-08:00","id":804332,"title":"","content":"Thanks for all the feedback!<br /> <br /> Finally I will do like Elsa and let it go. In the new and smaller city I will reduce both Covenants to a single NPC, just in case a player shows interest in the Circle or the Lancea. This way I will not close the door for me to create stories about them.<br /> <br /> I wil not change Circle of the Crone an inch, doing it would mutilate the game. If one of the new players shows interest in them I will try to depict them more appealing from the lore standpoint. Your tips gave me a lot of ideas at this respect.<br /> If sometime I decide to introduce a new form of blood magic, I will design a new Covenant.<br /> <br /> Last night I spoke with two of the new players and both would like to join... Ordo Dracul. Both are Masquerade veterans, and one of them has experience in Requiem. I asked why they choose the Ordo and they gave me this answers.<br /> The experienced player said &quot;if I were a vampire, the first thing I would do is try to overcome my dangerous limitations. Not get involved in politics or religion&quot;. He also likes the Dragon Coils.<br /> The new one: &quot;Well, the Invictus seems like the Camarilla. The Carthians like the Anarchs. The Circle and the Lancea like the Sabbath. Only the Ordo seems like really new to me&quot;.<br /> <br /> But no problem at all. I will present them the covenants in deep while playing because they will be just embraced vampires without Covenant. They will have time to know the covenants in deep before choosing one. They\u00b4re complex social structures hard to define properly in a few words. And like one of them said &quot;in game, the Covenant you choose relies a lot on what NPC you like or hate&quot;.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3008-masa","name":"Masa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3008_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T04:41:17-08:00","id":804362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Woland</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/803663-problem-with-religion-based-covenants-lancea-and-circle?p=804161#post804161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Moreover, you do not have to spend the rest of your unlife in some cave to get all that. No, you get to frequent the BEST parties, take the BEST drugs and have the BEST sexual experience you can imagine, because the Cronites know that sensuality is one of the most important parts of a sentient being. Forget all those boring Sanctified monks or stuck-up Ordo mentors - they keep you from it because they know that once someone tastes freedom, he will never again take their shit seriously.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, so Circle of Crone is vampiric Spring Court?! I never thought about running them this way, but it <b>does</b> make a lot of sense. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T04:41:41-08:00","id":804363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Masa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/803663-problem-with-religion-based-covenants-lancea-and-circle?p=804332#post804332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The new one: &quot;Well, the Invictus seems like the Camarilla. The Carthians like the Anarchs. The Circle and the Lancea like the Sabbath. Only the Ordo seems like really new to me&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>One thing of note, the ordo isn't actually new. The masquerade equivalent is actually the tzimisce following the path of metamorphosis. Minus the silliness about not sharing secrets.<br /> <br /> I think it's important to actually avoid making the covenant too appealing. The game is better served when there are no appealing choices. Or rather every covenant has it's good and bad points.<br /> <br /> The invictus are stability but they are also power hungry backstabbing schemers of the highest order. There is no loyalty in the invictus every vampire is a shark in a tiny pond.<br /> <br /> The carthians spout rethoric about democracy and representation that is superficaly very attractive to modern sensibility but when in power they act like the worse jackbooted 1984 thought police nightmare. Sure it's democracy, but there's only one party you're allowed to vote for and you'll lose your head if you don't toe the line. <br /> <br /> The lancea give you a sense of purpose and belonging, they're also utter sadistic monster who mentaly and physicly torture people to test their faith. To come to their attention is to become Job, except there is no doubling of wealth if you endure.<br /> <br /> The circle tell you to accept who you are but they exalt all the worse part of the vampiric experience. Sure the blood orgies are fun and game at first but things are less amusing when it's your touchstone strapped to the sacrifical altar whose heart is about to be ripped out for the glory of the dark mother.<br /> <br /> The ordo want to transcend the limitation of the vampiric condition but their methods are violent and at best torturous. Occultism and science uncoupled from any sort of ethical practice.<br /> <br /> there is a reason why joining any convenant and gaining status in them is a breaking point. These aren't clubs for good people to join as a way to deal with their condition. All of them are clubs for monster who revel in some aspect of their monstrosity.<br /> The humane vampire stays far away from them and is unaligned. Of course the humane vampire is a short lived vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2547-elderand","name":"Elderand","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"98"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T10:10:04-08:00","id":804520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elderand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/803663-problem-with-religion-based-covenants-lancea-and-circle?p=804363#post804363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">there is a reason why joining any convenant and gaining status in them is a breaking point. These aren't clubs for good people to join as a way to deal with their condition. All of them are clubs for monster who revel in some aspect of their monstrosity.<br /> The humane vampire stays far away from them and is unaligned. Of course the humane vampire is a short lived vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily disagreeing with you, but that is not the game as intended. Covenants are a means of coping with your condition that are supposed to hold you to some level of Humanity. They are means of emotional support as well as a kind of occupational therapy. Anything is better than just sharing your four walls alone with the Beast. The Covenants are a primary way to do this. The reason the covenants are unpleasant to mortal sensibilities is not that they are somehow inherently evil, but that they are made up of vampires. Science is not bad, but a vampire scientist has less scruples than a mortal one. Faith is not bad, but the Beast twists everything. Progress is not bad, but you got to watch out where you lead that change when your main motivation is selfish predation. The establishment is not bad, but an established alpha predator has to be merciless. An Unaligned Kindred has the problem of having to find their own way for how to handle their condition that does not involve becoming a monster in short order. It is not impossible, but you got to work for it. As page 31 of the Core says:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vampire: the Requiem Second Edition</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Dominican\">But the problem is that the one thing we can always do is hunt. <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Dominican\">And the vampire who only hunts, who times his existence based upon <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Dominican\">how long it is until he can next feed, becomes a hollowed-out, <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Dominican\">snarling monster at a truly terrifying rate. </span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>The Breaking Point for joining is not because you are joining an inherently inhuman or evil institution, but because you join a vampire institution. It is a kind of rite of passage from your former mortal life to your Requiem. The Unaligned simply ignores this step, possibly by fooling themselves a bit longer.<br /> <br /> The Curse, and by extension your Clan, is what drives you to be one of various kinds of monsters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T12:40:27-08:00","id":806337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Masa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/803663-problem-with-religion-based-covenants-lancea-and-circle?p=804332#post804332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Only the Ordo seems like really new to me&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div> The ordo is the bastard love child of the Tzim and Tremere with different powers! OH NO!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T10:56:28-08:00","id":810688,"title":"","content":"I fell in love with the circle... was looking through various requiem books trtying to find something that clicked... then found the Amanotsukai in the Circle of the crone book... Im an otaku for one thing... and the righteous mission of suffering in anothers place, as the unsang martyrs of the world... very apealing to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T13:09:28-08:00","id":810769,"title":"","content":"I'd just like to add that its perfectly ok to change either the circle or sanctified to be more appealing to players. By the nature of the game itself, each city in the world can have surprising differences within the same covenant. Perhaps a player wants the sanctified within his city to be less religious and more scholarly. You can even alter the core doctrine by saying vampires originate from Caine and that sanctum doctrines are based on the ancient writings of Caine. If the end result is that the sanctum still functions the same but ends up more appealing to players then go for it. Personal chronicles among friends are not official canon and therefore have no reason to follow canon if that is unappealing to players.<br /> <br /> All this said, if the vast majority of your players are interested in the Ordo then just make an Ordo focused chronicle. Theres nothing wrong with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8306-wissenschaft","name":"Wissenschaft","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T13:14:52-08:00","id":810776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Woland</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/803663-problem-with-religion-based-covenants-lancea-and-circle?p=804161#post804161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Moreover, you do not have to spend the rest of your unlife in some cave to get all that. No, you get to frequent the BEST parties, take the BEST drugs and have the BEST sexual experience you can imagine, because the Cronites know that sensuality is one of the most important parts of a sentient being. Forget all those boring Sanctified monks or stuck-up Ordo mentors - they keep you from it because they know that once someone tastes freedom, he will never again take their shit seriously.<br /> <br /> That way, you have the profit AND pleasure. If NPC the players care about are Cronites too, all the better. Believe me, portraying the Circle in my chronicle that way has worked wonders.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only problem with that is that vampires don't really have any sensuallity. Their walking corpses with deaden emotions where anything sex related is likely to boil down to a vampire gorging on blood. Of course, that might still be appealing to vampires. They are monsters after all and the circle is the only covenant that both fully embraces and isn't ashamed of being a vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8306,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8306-wissenschaft","user":"Wissenschaft","date":". 01-18-2016, 11:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8306-wissenschaft","name":"Wissenschaft","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T14:35:29-08:00","id":810819,"title":"","content":"Actually, they feel as acutely as you and me, probably more. Yeah sex kind of pales in comparison to feeding, but you can do both and sex is as good as it was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 01-17-2016, 05:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T15:33:02-08:00","id":810845,"title":"","content":"Well, no, sex isn't as good as it was for vampires. I'll just quote requiem for dummies rather then search through the corebooks:<br /> <br /> &quot;While the act of feeding replaces all physical urges, vampires can still indulge in sex and even take pleasure from it. Curiously, however, the emotional aspect of sex vanishes after the Embrace. A vampire might enjoy the physical sensation of sex, but no more than she enjoys a particularly savory smell or the touch of a luxurious fabric.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'd say that is a far cry from enjoying sex as good as it was. Besides, sex is a very human pleasure while the circle is about accepting ones vampiric nature. For the circle, having various &quot;feeding&quot; parties seems more appropriate than a religious orgy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8306,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8306-wissenschaft","user":"Wissenschaft","date":". 01-17-2016, 06:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8306-wissenschaft","name":"Wissenschaft","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T16:10:55-08:00","id":810860,"title":"","content":"Vampires don't have deadened emotions anymore. I haven't seen anything like that in 2e. As far as I know, it hasn't been a thing since Masquerade, but I skipped Requiem 1e. Is that &quot;Requiem for Dummies&quot; a 1e book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T16:20:12-08:00","id":810865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/803663-problem-with-religion-based-covenants-lancea-and-circle?p=810860#post810860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires don't have deadened emotions anymore. I haven't seen anything like that in 2e. As far as I know, it hasn't been a thing since Masquerade, but I skipped Requiem 1e. Is that &quot;Requiem for Dummies&quot; a 1e book?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, it is. I'm not sure if they don't have deaden emotions in 2e anymore or mention of emotions is just omitted entirely. That is one problem I have with 2e requiem. It tries to fit way too much into one book and the fluff on vampires suffers for it.<br /> <br /> Anyway, deaden emotions might be the wrong way to put it. It less that vampires lack emotions and more that everything pales in comparison to blood and feeding. I believe that much is the same in 2e. So my point stands, the circle is much more likely to hold feeding parties than religious orgies. Though to vampires those feeding parties are probably the same as orgies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8306,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8306-wissenschaft","user":"Wissenschaft","date":". 01-17-2016, 07:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8306-wissenschaft","name":"Wissenschaft","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T02:52:03-08:00","id":811046,"title":"","content":"I'm like 80% certain that I read a developer post that the emotional deadening was very explicitly not mentioned in 2e because they were walking it back so they could tell a wider variety of stories and that the characters could have more range, but it's 5am so I am not going to try to find a citation. Even if I was wrong, it's like most 1e material - it falls under the massive umbrella of &quot;Ask Your ST!&quot;. <br /> <br /> The only real suggestion I have is to look at how the fiction spread across the whole book portrays emotional reactions and sex. In my estimation, the Kindred involved REALLY get emotional and REALLY enjoy sex, but that's my reading.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T03:27:52-08:00","id":811048,"title":"","content":"The &quot;Vampires are emotionally dead&quot; thing got the chop when everyone realised that they were basically forcing the players into &quot;I don't have emotions, and that makes me feel sad&quot;. It just ruins the mood of the game because vampires were clinically incapable of giving a shit about their condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T06:07:42-08:00","id":811079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/803663-problem-with-religion-based-covenants-lancea-and-circle?p=811048#post811048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The &quot;Vampires are emotionally dead&quot; thing got the chop when everyone realised that they were basically forcing the players into &quot;I don't have emotions, and that makes me feel sad&quot;. It just ruins the mood of the game because vampires were clinically incapable of giving a shit about their condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, I exclusively play 1e and even I chop out the whole &quot;emotionally dead&quot; stuff from my games. I never understood why it was in there in the first place.<br /> <br /> Also, oddly enough, the Circle of the Crone is actually my favorite covenant, since we're on the topic of the religious covenants. The great thing about Requiem is that you can make any covenant or any aspect of the setting your own with little to no issue. The books actively encourage such behavior, unlike Masquerade.<br /> <br /> If you don't like how the Lancea Sanctum and Circle of the Crone are handled in-game, change them!<br /> <br /> I love Requiem, what can I say?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T08:26:28-08:00","id":811137,"title":"","content":"Ok, I stand corrected. lol<br /> <br /> Thats the benefits of not having an overarching metaplot. Requiem is more like a sandbox game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8306-wissenschaft","name":"Wissenschaft","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T13:18:04-08:00","id":811285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/803663-problem-with-religion-based-covenants-lancea-and-circle?p=811079#post811079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agreed, I exclusively play 1e and even I chop out the whole &amp;quot;emotionally dead&amp;quot; stuff from my games. I never understood why it was in there in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Carry over from Masquerade","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T03:11:51-08:00","id":811639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/803663-problem-with-religion-based-covenants-lancea-and-circle?p=811285#post811285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Carry over from Masquerade</div> </div> </div> </div>Thing is, I don't even remember that in Masquerade, unless it was added in during Revised Edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T04:00:13-08:00","id":811658,"title":"","content":"I miss the fishmalks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T04:20:35-08:00","id":811666,"title":"","content":"It was tied into the whole creative-sterility thing. Think of how Toreador supposedly adored music and art, but could never actually create masterpieces on their own. Technical skills, but no true &quot;heart&quot; to the peices. And probably a dash of gothic culture, that whole dead emotion thing was a popular idea for a while.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T04:43:17-08:00","id":811677,"title":"","content":"It adds to the atmosphere of damnation, because why wouldn't you go about eternity just creating marvelous pieces of artwork? That's the point. An eternity that can be actually fruitful isn't a damned one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T04:57:54-08:00","id":811688,"title":"","content":"It's not damned because of what you can do.. it's damned because of what you HAVE to do (seeing your family die/avoiding the sun/having to drink the blood of the living..)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T05:06:19-08:00","id":811691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/803663-problem-with-religion-based-covenants-lancea-and-circle?p=811688#post811688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not damned because of what you can do.. it's damned because of what you HAVE to do (seeing your family die/avoiding the sun/having to drink the blood of the living..)</div> </div> </div> </div>There can be multiple levels to damnation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T05:26:12-08:00","id":811701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/803663-problem-with-religion-based-covenants-lancea-and-circle?p=811688#post811688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not damned because of what you can do.. it's damned because of what you HAVE to do (seeing your family die/avoiding the sun/having to drink the blood of the living..)</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are tragic at the start. Then you get used to it, then you try to figure out what to do with your endless time. And producing things of lasting value isn't one of those things.<br /> <br /> It's one of the ways we deal with tragedy. You mourn, then you process, then you channel it into something productive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T18:34:22-08:00","id":813071,"title":"","content":"Maybe I'm just confusing the moral decay of elders as their humanity drops as the ages past by. lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8306-wissenschaft","name":"Wissenschaft","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T05:09:40-08:00","id":813295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wissenschaft</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/803663-problem-with-religion-based-covenants-lancea-and-circle?p=813071#post813071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe I'm just confusing the moral decay of elders as their humanity drops as the ages past by. lol</div> </div> </div> </div> Elders don't necessarily lose morals. They do stop thinking like a human, but they can still hold to ethical and personal moral standards no matter their Humanity level. Just because you're a monster doesn't mean you can't be a noble one.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T14:28:03-08:00","id":813654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/803663-problem-with-religion-based-covenants-lancea-and-circle?p=813295#post813295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Elders don't necessarily lose morals. They do stop thinking like a human, but they can still hold to ethical and personal moral standards no matter their Humanity level. Just because you're a monster doesn't mean you can't be a noble one.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't know how noble humanity 4 vampires then to be but I assume not much. That said, yes, just because your an elder doesn't mean you have low humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8306-wissenschaft","name":"Wissenschaft","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T15:33:02-08:00","id":813698,"title":"","content":"That's just it. Low Humanity and nobility are not mutually exclusive. That's the point I'm making.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T16:22:49-08:00","id":813734,"title":"","content":"You can be a super nice guy and have abismal Humanity, it happens. The opposite is true too, You can have an abosuletly horrible monster with high Humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T19:55:15-08:00","id":813853,"title":"","content":"In my opinion if your players don't like a particular group, and especially if the ST doesn't either, then that just makes that group the perfect candidates for party antagonists. Just take the worst possible version of that group and go to town. If your players don't think much of Cruac sorcery, let them feel the weight of its power used against them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T02:42:40-08:00","id":814009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Masa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/803663-problem-with-religion-based-covenants-lancea-and-circle?p=804332#post804332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for all the feedback!<br /> <br /> Finally I will do like Elsa and let it go. In the new and smaller city I will reduce both Covenants to a single NPC, just in case a player shows interest in the Circle or the Lancea. This way I will not close the door for me to create stories about them.<br /> <br /> I wil not change Circle of the Crone an inch, doing it would mutilate the game. If one of the new players shows interest in them I will try to depict them more appealing from the lore standpoint. Your tips gave me a lot of ideas at this respect.<br /> If sometime I decide to introduce a new form of blood magic, I will design a new Covenant.<br /> <br /> Last night I spoke with two of the new players and both would like to join... Ordo Dracul. Both are Masquerade veterans, and one of them has experience in Requiem. I asked why they choose the Ordo and they gave me this answers.<br /> The experienced player said &quot;if I were a vampire, the first thing I would do is try to overcome my dangerous limitations. Not get involved in politics or religion&quot;. He also likes the Dragon Coils.<br /> The new one: &quot;Well, the Invictus seems like the Camarilla. The Carthians like the Anarchs. The Circle and the Lancea like the Sabbath. Only the Ordo seems like really new to me&quot;.<br /> <br /> But no problem at all. I will present them the covenants in deep while playing because they will be just embraced vampires without Covenant. They will have time to know the covenants in deep before choosing one. They\u00b4re complex social structures hard to define properly in a few words. And like one of them said &quot;in game, the Covenant you choose relies a lot on what NPC you like or hate&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>It sounds to me like some of what you have issues with is how popular the ordo is being with your players, right?<br /> <br /> If you're willing to use some of the other covenants mentioned some of your players might bite. In Danse Macabre there are additional covenants- a biker gang, a cult, a group that gets warnings of the future from the God-Machine, a group that infects its members with the minds of their leaders to fight the Beast, a group that can't bloodbond their ghouls so their ghouls are more than equal partners, and a group that can travel anywhere in the world through mirrors thanks to the patronage of Bloody Mary.<br /> <br /> In mythologies there's a covenant of Sin-eaters (not geist possessed vampires, but vampires who know how to consume the sins of mortals as well as blood.<br /> <br /> And in Dark Eras the vampire section has the premiere covenant being a group of &quot;witches&quot; who have a network of tit for tat favor system set up with other supernaturals ranging from other pc types to even saints and cosmic principles.<br /> <br /> So if it's something new and different that your players are looking for, perhaps someone who has Death on speed dial would do it, or a courier who could be halfway across the world as long as they have a mirror and a cell phone handy (mirror travel works by two vampires forging a portal between them), a vampire who has an amoral vampire elder in his head as his own personal jiminy cricket or a vampire who gets messages from the future, etc, might scratch that itch.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T05:34:24-08:00","id":814064,"title":"","content":"The way I'd do it is to make more (if not most) kindred members of more than one covenant. Two are political &quot;parties&quot;, two are religions, and one is a secret society. Being a member of the Invictus and a member of the Lancea Sanctum should be no weirder than being a Democrat and a Southern Baptist at the same time. This also has the benefit of boosting memberships in the groups in small cities and of making dynamics more complex (&quot;sure, he's Invictus but he's one of those weirdo blood cult Invictus, not like us&quot;). With the covenants not, by default, being exclusive, the player doesn't feel like they are giving up taking part in the more popular covenants by choosing one of the others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T21:33:02-08:00","id":815890,"title":"","content":"Covenants are already not exclusive, the limit is 5 points in covenant status, so technically a vampire could be a member of five different covenants at the same time.<br /> <br /> I imagine they would be seen as terribly flighty though. <br /> <br /> Oh yes, I forgot a covenant from danse macabre- a group of necromancers who can feed off of the death energy of other death aligned supernaturals. Weird that I did that, I thought they were one of the more interesting additions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}